{
  "id": "maf-parse-into-packer",
  "measured": "2026-09-28",
  "published": false,
  "source": {
    "kind": "bench",
    "repro": "npx esbuild plugins/maf/benches/mafOnMarks.bench.ts --bundle --platform=node --format=esm --outfile=/tmp/mafOnMarks.mjs --banner:js=\"import { createRequire } from 'module'; const require = createRequire(import.meta.url);\" && for a in tabix bigmaf; do for s in 0 1 2; do node --expose-gc --max-old-space-size=12000 /tmp/mafOnMarks.mjs --parse --adapter=$a --shape=$s --rounds=20 --json; done; done",
    "notes": "On ada (24 cores, load 3-21 across the runs), one process per shape and adapter, two passes, MIN across both passes' rounds. Every arm reads the region off the adapter over a warm chunk cache, parse included. The MAF display's arms are the worker's half of LinearMafGetAlignmentData: the blocks into a MafRegionSink, finishBlocks and buildMafCoverageRegion. Features reads MafFeatures (getFeatures into the sink, as every adapter did before readBlocks); control is the same declared again; direct is the adapter's readBlocks. The mark display's arms are marks_maf_cells: the adapter's table (over MafFeatures, or getFeatureTable's direct parse), layerTables and the columnar encoder with no hit index. Read is the BED or bigBed read alone. A collection before each arm (--expose-gc), interleaved round-robin with the order rotated, and the direct packed wire and encoded lanes checked equal to the features' before timing. The bigMaf fixture is the MAF-tabix one's blocks as s lines, built with bedToBigBed."
  },
